From: MCC45TR <75160848+MCC45TR@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: keep the Cliffs video configuration clocks enabled

The exact Uke OEM gcc-cliffs.c enables the video AHB and XO gates at
0x32004 and 0x32030 before registering GCC. The current upstream SM8650
driver does the same for this shared block. Restore only those video
gates, retaining the separate camera, display and GPU clock policy.

On Uke 7.3.0-6 both CBCRs read 0x80000000 and MVS0C never reaches the
power-up-complete state. Clock registration alone does not enable these
unexported gates. Propagate each regmap failure before exposing GCC.

OEM: MiCode 5712080a4b0c0b1a879e6d145c601c649ddaddfd,
drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c (GPL-2.0-only).
This source correction requires a separate native power/firmware trial.

---
diff --git a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c
--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/gcc-cliffs.c
@@ -3171,7 +3171,15 @@ static int gcc_cliffs_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	if (IS_ERR(regmap))
 		return PTR_ERR(regmap);
 
-	/* USB data bring-up does not force camera/display/GPU/video gates. */
+	/* OEM requires both configuration gates before any video GDSC access. */
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, 0x32004, BIT(0), BIT(0));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	ret = regmap_update_bits(regmap, 0x32030, BIT(0), BIT(0));
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+
+	/* Video bring-up does not force camera/display/GPU gates. */
 	ret = clk_vdd_proxy_vote(&pdev->dev, &gcc_cliffs_desc);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
